From: fish <lunarisfelix02@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] op7t-0172: Bluetooth: firmware from bluetooth_a, a small FAT reader

0171 booted (2026-11-11 00:07, 7 GiB): version and reset answered as
before, the file number came out 11 as meant, but "image/crbtfw11.tlv:
not on the modem partition": the BT files are on the bluetooth_a
partition (backup/wifi-files.txt, section "== bluetooth_a"), not on
modem_a. SweetModem's FAT index is the modem's own (it serves the modem's
file requests at run time), so sweet_bt.c gets its own minimal read-only
reader on sweet_ufs_read_part("bluetooth_a", ...): FAT12/16/32, short 8.3
names (IMAGE/CRBTFW11.TLV, IMAGE/CRNV11.BIN), cluster chains. Logs the
volume ("FAT%u, N-byte clusters"); the rest of 0171 is unchanged.

Apply after 0171.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c
index 3693192..63f2510 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_bt.c
@@ -25,8 +25,8 @@
  *     event 0xFF: cresp 0, rtype 2, product id, patch, ROM version, SoC id) and HCI_Reset; every
  *     byte that comes back is logged, and the ROM version and SoC id are decoded.
